# ibl.ai Chrome extension — build-time configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored) and run `pnpm ext:build`. Vite reads
# .env / .env.local from THIS directory, so only `VITE_`-prefixed keys reach the
# panel, and only at build time — there is nothing to configure at runtime.
#
# A build with no .env.local is the production build: MENTOR_URL falls back to
# https://os.ibl.ai. That is what CI publishes to the Chrome Web Store.

# The web app the side panel loads in its iframe.
# Unset -> https://os.ibl.ai. For local development against `pnpm dev`:
VITE_MENTOR_URL=http://localhost:3000

# The build writes this host's origin into the manifest's `frame-src` and
# `child-src` (it replaces __MENTOR_ORIGIN__ in public/manifest.json), so any
# host you point this at is framed rather than blocked by CSP.
#
# The platform hosts are a separate matter and are not configurable here:
# PLATFORM_DOMAIN (src/settings.ts) and AUTH_URL (src/auth.ts) are constants, the
# manifest's host_permissions pin the same two domains, and a platform outside
# *.iblai.app / *.ibl.ai needs its DM hosts added to `connect-src` by hand.
